  "notes": "The isolated letters (1:1) are not glossed. A book for «كتاب» (it leaves before «إليك»); light for «من الظلمات إلى النور بإذن ربهم» (after «لتخرج»; no plate on the Prophet ﷺ), geometric for «العزيز الحميد» and «الله الذي له ما في السماوات». A falling leaf for «الحياة الدنيا», two paths for «ويبغونها عوجا». Nothing drawn for the punishment (2:10-14). STAGING v4: c1 (1) stays ambient: the Book revealed to the Prophet ﷺ to bring people out of darkness into light (his mission; quiet over 1:3-6 and 1:11-16, no plate on him); plates unchanged. c2 (2-3): a market by day. Geometric for Allah to whom belongs what is in the heavens and the earth (2:1-9); the camera closes on three men in dark robes for woe to the disbelievers (2:10, the threat held on them). They sit down among the stalls as those who prefer the worldly life over the Hereafter (3:2, a falling-leaf plate for the worldly life, 3:3-6), and speak to three other townspeople (3:7, they avert people from Allah's way: As-Sa'di, they avert people); the townspeople make no gesture (nobody is shown being turned away). Two paths for they seek to make it crooked (3:11-12); the camera closes on the dark-robed men for in far error (3:13). No women: the blamed group and the townspeople are three men each."
